\cb3 \ul What is it?\cb1 \ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Roam-A-Dome (RAD) allows you to set a home position for your dome, random seek/left right, and to send serial commands to change the position of the dome.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 It works with either gear or rubber wheel setups and any droid control system (Shadow/Padawan/Stealth/Kyber/etc). Supported motors are either using Syren packet serial or PWM control. The RAD controller sits between the motor controller and your droid control system (Shadow/Kyber/etc). It passes through the motor output from your droid control system to always allow for full manual control, but when the controller is idle it will allow for automated animations such as sending the dome to a home position, random seek/left right, shake head, spin head, etc.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 RAD controller comes in two flavors. A compact controller and an OLED controller. The function identically except for the OLED controller has a display that shows the current dome position and goes to sleep if the dome is idle.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 There is also an optional battery powered remote that allows you to adjust your dome settings remotely (battery not included).\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
